target: cmd/looper/main.go
verify: go test ./cmd/looper/ -count=1 -run 'TestPushCheckWritesTheDiagnosisToStderr'
expect: want the diagnosis
why:    the diagnosis exists in internal/push and is tested there, but the one line handing it a stream lives here. Dropping it leaves the library fully covered and the BINARY — the only thing Step 14 ever runs — silent about the one refusal whose stated reason is wrong for the actual cause. Measured: deleting this field left `go test ./...` entirely green, including all four subtests of TestCheckDiagnosesBeingUnableToAsk — the one test written for the feature — none of which went through the CLI. nil is the documented "no diagnosis" value, so this compiles and changes only what the operator sees.
--- old
		Diag:           errOut,
--- new
		Diag:           nil,
